1
00:00:37,954 --> 00:00:43,250
In the 19th century, as America expanded
across the vast continent,

2
00:00:43,251 --> 00:00:46,963
the frontier was, without a doubt,
the conquest of the West.

3
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:53,219
To the West…

4
00:00:57,098 --> 00:00:59,893
a desire called America
crossed the continent…

5
00:01:02,937 --> 00:01:05,315
consuming the lands of the native people

6
00:01:06,232 --> 00:01:08,318
and reaching the Pacific Ocean.

7
00:01:18,203 --> 00:01:20,245
Punish him! We must punish him!

8
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:23,416
He had the white man's books
hidden in his tent!

9
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:34,344
What's with that way of running?

10
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:37,097
That's how white men run!

11
00:01:39,432 --> 00:01:41,226
He disappeared?!

12
00:01:45,105 --> 00:01:50,860
And in the summer of 1890,
people began to gather in the wilderness,

13
00:01:51,611 --> 00:01:57,450
where the Santa Ana headwinds blow
from Mexico, in search of something.

14
00:02:06,918 --> 00:02:11,422
EPISODE 1
STEEL BALL RUN

15
00:02:14,968 --> 00:02:17,636
Hey! The toilet's overflowing with poop!

16
00:02:17,637 --> 00:02:19,888
- This is my tent!
- Shut up, I was here first!

17
00:02:19,889 --> 00:02:21,265
SEPTEMBER 23, 1890
SAN DIEGO BEACH

18
00:02:21,266 --> 00:02:24,102
Welcome to the Steel Ball Run race!

19
00:02:28,064 --> 00:02:33,152
This race starts here
in San Diego and ends in New York.

20
00:02:33,153 --> 00:02:39,159
This is the first-ever horseback race
across the North American continent!

21
00:02:41,953 --> 00:02:44,746
The total distance is about 4,000 miles.

22
00:02:44,747 --> 00:02:47,875
The course is divided into nine stages,

23
00:02:47,876 --> 00:02:52,130
and the prize money
for conquering it is $50 million.

24
00:02:53,006 --> 00:02:58,553
Only one of the people gathered
on the beach right now will claim it.

25
00:03:01,973 --> 00:03:03,765
Mr. Steven Steel!

26
00:03:03,766 --> 00:03:08,937
Baron Roocatugo from Germany announced
he'd use a machine called an automobile.

27
00:03:08,938 --> 00:03:10,815
I approved it, of course.

28
00:03:11,482 --> 00:03:14,777
The spirit of pioneering is
part of this race's identity.

29
00:03:15,612 --> 00:03:19,823
No matter what kind of machine it is,
we'll take on this challenge.

30
00:03:19,824 --> 00:03:24,703
There's criticism that the $150 entry fee
is a money-seeking scheme.

31
00:03:24,704 --> 00:03:26,456
I don't think so.

32
00:03:27,332 --> 00:03:30,334
Because we'll cover medical
and other expenses

33
00:03:30,335 --> 00:03:32,544
if a participant retires.

34
00:03:32,545 --> 00:03:36,465
However, they must ensure
their own safety during the race.

35
00:03:36,466 --> 00:03:42,262
We won't violate the Second Amendment
right to bear arms and protect oneself.

36
00:03:42,263 --> 00:03:45,767
The race will be a total failure
if no one reaches the goal.

37
00:03:46,267 --> 00:03:49,395
How will you take responsibility
toward the investors?

38
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:52,190
I might get killed.

39
00:03:52,815 --> 00:03:54,442
Just kidding.

40
00:03:55,151 --> 00:03:56,444
Excuse me?

41
00:03:57,111 --> 00:03:59,279
Failure is…

42
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:00,906
Listen carefully!

43
00:04:00,907 --> 00:04:04,826
True failure is when
someone forgets the pioneering spirit

44
00:04:04,827 --> 00:04:09,415
and stays away
from ever facing challenges!

45
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:13,461
In this race,
there's no such thing as failure!

46
00:04:13,962 --> 00:04:16,213
All we've got are adventurers!

47
00:04:16,214 --> 00:04:18,966
This Steel Ball Run race
will be a competition

48
00:04:18,967 --> 00:04:24,138
that no one in the world
has ever experienced before!

49
00:04:29,185 --> 00:04:34,523
What do I do? I'm so worried, you know?

50
00:04:34,524 --> 00:04:38,194
What do I do if it fails?

51
00:04:38,695 --> 00:04:40,821
Don't worry, Steven.

52
00:04:40,822 --> 00:04:44,117
You've been a promoter
for 40 years, haven't you?

53
00:04:45,118 --> 00:04:48,663
Have confidence, my dear.

54
00:04:51,082 --> 00:04:53,126
Okay, I'll do my best.

55
00:04:53,626 --> 00:04:54,919
There, there.

56
00:05:07,098 --> 00:05:09,851
You'd like to participate
in the race, correct?

57
00:05:11,519 --> 00:05:12,979
Please sign here.

58
00:05:13,563 --> 00:05:17,025
We'll take the horse's noseprint
and the racer's fingerprints on race day.

59
00:05:17,525 --> 00:05:21,070
The rider and the horse
cannot be replaced during the race.

60
00:05:21,571 --> 00:05:23,740
This is your entry certificate
and saddlecloth.

61
00:05:31,039 --> 00:05:32,999
Gyro Zeppeli.

62
00:05:34,709 --> 00:05:36,878
He-heh!

63
00:05:38,588 --> 00:05:41,758
That's a strange thing you've got there.

64
00:05:42,342 --> 00:05:44,802
What do you use these for?

65
00:05:46,304 --> 00:05:48,014
WHIRL

66
00:05:48,848 --> 00:05:49,682
What the…

67
00:05:54,312 --> 00:05:56,521
What? My legs…

68
00:05:56,522 --> 00:05:59,483
You bastard! What did you do?

69
00:05:59,484 --> 00:06:03,153
I was just a little curious
about those weird things.

70
00:06:03,154 --> 00:06:04,488
Is that so?

71
00:06:04,489 --> 00:06:07,700
Attendant, count my entry fee.

72
00:06:08,451 --> 00:06:12,705
If there's nothing wrong,
I'll believe what you say.

73
00:06:15,083 --> 00:06:17,751
Oh, you're $20 short.

74
00:06:17,752 --> 00:06:20,004
But I certainly paid, didn't I?

75
00:06:20,505 --> 00:06:24,591
I haven't issued the receipt yet.
If it's short, it's short.

76
00:06:24,592 --> 00:06:27,552
Then I knew it. It was you.

77
00:06:27,553 --> 00:06:30,472
Take out the coins you pocketed.

78
00:06:30,473 --> 00:06:36,854
Otherwise, I won't be able
to enter the race and win, will I?

79
00:06:38,481 --> 00:06:39,982
What, a thief?

80
00:06:40,483 --> 00:06:42,025
Security!

81
00:06:42,026 --> 00:06:43,736
Give me my receipt first.

82
00:06:51,869 --> 00:06:54,372
- What's going on?
- They say he's a pickpocket.

83
00:06:56,290 --> 00:06:58,459
Valkyrie, sorry to keep you waiting.

84
00:06:59,544 --> 00:07:02,295
- Now, which tent is mine--
- Hey!

85
00:07:02,296 --> 00:07:06,299
Stop right there, you bastard!
This isn't over!

86
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:10,053
Don't get cocky
pulling weird shit like that.

87
00:07:10,054 --> 00:07:11,139
Stay still!

88
00:07:11,931 --> 00:07:14,142
You're dead!

89
00:07:15,393 --> 00:07:17,269
Hey, this idiot took my gun.

90
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:18,521
You bastard!

91
00:07:21,732 --> 00:07:26,028
Hey, gold-teeth bastard.
If I wanted, you'd be dead right now.

92
00:07:26,654 --> 00:07:30,657
You never saw the moment
I took your money.

93
00:07:30,658 --> 00:07:33,910
You took a random guess
and tried to embarrass me!

94
00:07:33,911 --> 00:07:35,996
I can't let this slide anymore!

95
00:07:35,997 --> 00:07:40,876
I've decided! I'll join the race
and follow you all the way!

96
00:07:40,877 --> 00:07:43,712
Shut up!
We're turning you in to the sheriff.

97
00:07:43,713 --> 00:07:45,923
Let that guy go.

98
00:07:47,675 --> 00:07:49,426
I'm not pressing charges.

99
00:07:49,427 --> 00:07:51,637
Complaint withdrawn. Let him go.

100
00:07:53,514 --> 00:07:56,142
And give him the gun back.

101
00:08:11,032 --> 00:08:12,074
Pick it up.

102
00:08:12,950 --> 00:08:16,579
But once you do, that'll be the signal.

103
00:08:21,459 --> 00:08:23,001
We can't handle this.

104
00:08:23,002 --> 00:08:24,085
Get the sheriff!

105
00:08:24,086 --> 00:08:26,631
They might end up killing each other!

106
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:29,174
What's all this noise?

107
00:08:29,175 --> 00:08:32,052
Hey! Move it, guys.

108
00:08:32,053 --> 00:08:33,471
I can't see.

109
00:08:42,605 --> 00:08:44,564
Hey!

110
00:08:44,565 --> 00:08:46,983
Why did you take it so seriously?

111
00:08:46,984 --> 00:08:49,028
I was just kidding, just kidding!

112
00:08:50,029 --> 00:08:53,574
Come on, don't make such a scary face.

113
00:08:54,659 --> 00:08:57,953
See? It was all a joke.

114
00:08:57,954 --> 00:09:00,455
Anyway, good luck in the race.

115
00:09:00,456 --> 00:09:03,251
What are you guys doing here?

116
00:09:04,544 --> 00:09:06,462
THUD

117
00:09:17,598 --> 00:09:19,350
I'm not a nice guy.

118
00:09:19,976 --> 00:09:22,561
Get your finger off the trigger.

119
00:09:22,562 --> 00:09:26,440
Then get yourself to a hospital.
Make it before lunch.

120
00:09:28,276 --> 00:09:30,486
You goddamn bastard!

121
00:09:39,453 --> 00:09:41,371
Sheriff, what do we do?

122
00:09:41,372 --> 00:09:44,333
It's nothing. Just a duel.

123
00:09:44,959 --> 00:09:48,379
A duel both sides agreed to.
Nothing wrong with that.

124
00:09:49,922 --> 00:09:51,673
A duel?

125
00:09:51,674 --> 00:09:54,385
What did that guy just do?

126
00:09:55,136 --> 00:09:58,096
That Steel Ball was spinning.

127
00:09:58,097 --> 00:09:59,014
THUD

128
00:09:59,015 --> 00:10:00,181
And fast.

129
00:10:00,182 --> 00:10:04,729
And it dug into his arm
and kept spinning even more.

130
00:10:06,105 --> 00:10:08,983
Hey, you! What is that Steel Ball?

131
00:10:09,483 --> 00:10:11,192
Let me see it again!

132
00:10:11,193 --> 00:10:13,195
Don't touch it! It's still spinning!

133
00:10:25,291 --> 00:10:27,668
What just happened?

134
00:10:28,169 --> 00:10:32,590
Just now,
I really was standing on my own legs.

135
00:10:36,927 --> 00:10:38,387
Wait!

136
00:10:39,847 --> 00:10:40,973
Let me through!

137
00:10:41,724 --> 00:10:44,768
Out of my way! Move it, you slow punk!

138
00:10:44,769 --> 00:10:46,936
- What did you just say?
- Shut up!

139
00:10:46,937 --> 00:10:48,356
Wait!

140
00:10:50,232 --> 00:10:53,068
Tell me! What did you just do to me?

141
00:10:53,069 --> 00:10:54,736
What just happened?

142
00:10:54,737 --> 00:10:57,406
Do you know the top cause of death?

143
00:10:58,282 --> 00:11:01,576
Diseases spread by mosquitoes
are number one,

144
00:11:01,577 --> 00:11:04,455
then getting kicked by a horse.

145
00:11:04,955 --> 00:11:08,167
Are you trying to switch those rankings?

146
00:11:08,751 --> 00:11:10,878
Don't get any weird hopes up.

147
00:11:11,587 --> 00:11:15,048
You standing up from that chair
was just a coincidence.

148
00:11:15,049 --> 00:11:17,217
It was only a physical reflex.

149
00:11:17,218 --> 00:11:18,094
A reflex?

150
00:11:19,136 --> 00:11:21,180
So it really was the Steel Ball!

151
00:11:22,056 --> 00:11:24,391
Show it again! I'll pay you for it.

152
00:11:24,392 --> 00:11:26,769
I'm done talking.

153
00:11:34,026 --> 00:11:37,779
Hey, brat.
You really had the nerve to do that.

154
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:39,280
Well?

155
00:11:39,281 --> 00:11:40,157
In that case…

156
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:46,872
I'll go ahead and touch it again myself!

157
00:11:56,090 --> 00:11:57,424
My fingers…

158
00:11:57,425 --> 00:12:00,302
I'll give you credit
before disappointing you.

159
00:12:00,803 --> 00:12:05,140
You've got some well-trained muscles
in your upper body.

160
00:12:05,141 --> 00:12:07,143
Now, let me make this clear.

161
00:12:07,643 --> 00:12:13,231
The Steel Spin won't make someone
who can't walk start walking again.

162
00:12:13,232 --> 00:12:15,859
Like, I'd buy that
with all that's happened!

163
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:19,320
I swear I'll uncover
the truth behind that spin!

164
00:12:19,321 --> 00:12:21,656
Even though you can't ride a horse?

165
00:12:21,657 --> 00:12:23,909
I'll be gone the day after tomorrow.

166
00:12:24,577 --> 00:12:26,786
I've got a race to win.

167
00:12:26,787 --> 00:12:29,206
Hey, wait! Damn it…

168
00:12:36,005 --> 00:12:37,631
Move it! Out of my way!

169
00:12:38,632 --> 00:12:41,551
Don't come around here, you trash.

170
00:12:41,552 --> 00:12:44,096
Hurry up and go home now.

171
00:13:02,948 --> 00:13:05,701
I wonder why I came to this beach.

172
00:13:07,411 --> 00:13:11,081
Was it simply
to see the start of the race?

173
00:13:11,707 --> 00:13:12,833
Or something else?

174
00:13:16,962 --> 00:13:19,381
My name is Johnny Joestar.

175
00:13:19,882 --> 00:13:23,594
My father was a rancher
and a famous horse trainer.

176
00:13:24,094 --> 00:13:27,765
From the day I was born,
horses have always been by my side.

177
00:13:29,517 --> 00:13:32,227
Seeing the horse's muscles move
atop the saddle

178
00:13:32,228 --> 00:13:35,898
and hearing the hooves
strike the ground felt beautiful to me.

179
00:13:36,398 --> 00:13:42,071
Through their running, I felt like I could
understand horses' thoughts and emotions.

180
00:13:44,406 --> 00:13:46,784
People love beautiful things.

181
00:13:47,284 --> 00:13:52,248
And if that beautiful thing is in motion,
then it's the most beautiful thing ever.

182
00:13:53,165 --> 00:13:55,251
"Young Master Johnny has talent,"

183
00:13:55,835 --> 00:13:58,670
said an old groom, and I got encouraged.

184
00:13:58,671 --> 00:14:01,215
But my father never cared about me.

185
00:14:02,049 --> 00:14:05,469
My older brother Nicholas
was already in the spotlight.

186
00:14:07,054 --> 00:14:10,140
But one day, he died in an accident.

187
00:14:11,392 --> 00:14:13,143
Everything changed.

188
00:14:15,145 --> 00:14:16,479
After my brother's death,

189
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:20,149
I began racing seriously,
winning over and over again.

190
00:14:20,150 --> 00:14:22,278
I was called a prodigy.

191
00:14:23,779 --> 00:14:27,156
With each victory,
more people gathered around me,

192
00:14:27,157 --> 00:14:30,828
flattering me from under the horse,
bringing money and gifts.

193
00:14:31,829 --> 00:14:34,038
Winning on horseback

194
00:14:34,039 --> 00:14:39,044
was a symbol of triumph
in human history and a mark of authority.

195
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:43,090
But it didn't last long.

196
00:14:43,591 --> 00:14:47,969
So you know, Dorothy Parker is super cute!

197
00:14:47,970 --> 00:14:49,888
You really love her, don't you?

198
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:54,642
I'm telling you, the time's coming
when cool actresses become art!

199
00:14:54,643 --> 00:14:58,438
- Excuse me, I'm standing in line.
- Man, look at this crowd.

200
00:14:58,439 --> 00:14:59,607
Oh really?

201
00:15:01,442 --> 00:15:03,610
I've been here since yesterday.

202
00:15:03,611 --> 00:15:05,361
Wow, that's amazing.

203
00:15:05,362 --> 00:15:10,033
The back of the line is over there!
I've been here all night!

204
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:13,328
Shut up!
You're shaking after a single all-nighter!

205
00:15:13,329 --> 00:15:15,496
Hey, what's going on here?

206
00:15:15,497 --> 00:15:20,002
Hey, I was standing in line properly,
but this guy started giving me crap.

207
00:15:20,502 --> 00:15:23,255
This is Johnny Joestar.

208
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:29,636
I knew it! You're the coolest.

209
00:15:29,637 --> 00:15:31,930
But is this worth lining up for?

210
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:33,640
Well…

211
00:15:33,641 --> 00:15:34,683
BAM

212
00:15:35,517 --> 00:15:36,560
What's up?

213
00:15:37,144 --> 00:15:39,188
You're one persistent bastard.

214
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:47,446
What the hell did you…

215
00:15:52,451 --> 00:15:54,578
Once again, everything changed.

216
00:16:00,876 --> 00:16:02,419
Hey, nurse.

217
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:05,047
Answer me! Hey!

218
00:16:06,215 --> 00:16:08,509
Crap… Damn it…

219
00:16:09,218 --> 00:16:15,057
It's mine…
I'm shitting myself, and pissing too…

220
00:16:15,557 --> 00:16:20,813
Hey, hurry up and clean up my shit!
That's your job, isn't it?

221
00:16:21,313 --> 00:16:24,315
And what's this tube hooked up to my leg?

222
00:16:24,316 --> 00:16:26,110
Blood's flowing through it!

223
00:16:28,654 --> 00:16:31,240
Stop yelling so loudly.

224
00:16:32,366 --> 00:16:35,118
I'm just taking some of your blood.

225
00:16:35,119 --> 00:16:38,579
You can't feel anything anyway,
so it's fine, isn't it?

226
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:39,915
You bastard…

227
00:16:42,710 --> 00:16:46,045
No one comes to visit you.

228
00:16:46,046 --> 00:16:48,090
Not even your old man.

229
00:16:48,841 --> 00:16:51,343
No one wants to look at you.

230
00:16:51,927 --> 00:16:56,765
You're just some former jockey prodigy
who can't even clean up his own shit!

231
00:17:00,019 --> 00:17:01,770
Damn it.

232
00:17:02,813 --> 00:17:05,107
I'll find out, no matter what.

233
00:17:05,607 --> 00:17:07,776
I'll ride a horse again!

234
00:17:08,277 --> 00:17:11,655
SEPTEMBER 24, 1890
THE DAY BEFORE THE RACE

235
00:17:13,282 --> 00:17:17,411
How is it, Valkyrie? See any horses
that could potentially rival you?

236
00:17:17,995 --> 00:17:20,205
From what I can see…

237
00:17:27,588 --> 00:17:29,380
He's seriously still going?

238
00:17:29,381 --> 00:17:31,340
He's been at it since midnight.

239
00:17:31,341 --> 00:17:33,718
I heard he's going to enter the race.

240
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:38,765
But no matter how much of a famous jockey
he used to be, that's just sad.

241
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:40,517
For the horse, that is.

242
00:17:42,853 --> 00:17:44,645
SLAM

243
00:17:44,646 --> 00:17:46,482
Hey, he's in trouble.

244
00:17:47,066 --> 00:17:49,567
Is he still dreaming about his past glory?

245
00:17:49,568 --> 00:17:51,445
He'll get seriously hurt.

246
00:17:55,199 --> 00:17:57,618
Yikes! Is that guy really okay?

247
00:17:58,494 --> 00:18:01,996
I heard he can't feel pain
'cause of what happened to his lower body.

248
00:18:01,997 --> 00:18:07,294
On top of that, the horse he was sold is
old, bad-tempered, and out of control.

249
00:18:08,462 --> 00:18:09,463
Watch.

250
00:18:12,299 --> 00:18:14,717
I can't watch this! Tell him to stop!

251
00:18:14,718 --> 00:18:16,178
You think so too, right?

252
00:18:17,012 --> 00:18:19,223
I was just watching.

253
00:18:19,723 --> 00:18:23,685
But if you ask me,
there's no way he's riding that thing.

254
00:18:24,269 --> 00:18:26,188
He can't ride it like that.

255
00:18:27,856 --> 00:18:32,861
To put it another way, if he could ride
that thing, he'd be beyond human.

256
00:18:36,573 --> 00:18:38,117
I want to join the race.

257
00:18:39,409 --> 00:18:41,869
Listen, you need to pay an entry fee.

258
00:18:41,870 --> 00:18:43,705
With the white man's money.

259
00:18:44,748 --> 00:18:46,875
Can you pay?

260
00:18:48,085 --> 00:18:49,169
This is…

261
00:18:50,212 --> 00:18:51,630
An emerald?

262
00:18:53,298 --> 00:18:55,424
Your certificate and saddlecloth.

263
00:18:55,425 --> 00:18:58,427
Before the start,
we'll take your horse's noseprint.

264
00:18:58,428 --> 00:19:00,806
- No need.
- What?

265
00:19:01,723 --> 00:19:05,853
I'll cross the continent
and win with just these legs.

266
00:19:07,146 --> 00:19:10,315
All I need is the white man's money.

267
00:19:15,988 --> 00:19:17,739
Tomorrow is finally the day.

268
00:19:30,878 --> 00:19:33,797
SEPTEMBER 25, 1890
RACE DAY

269
00:19:45,142 --> 00:19:46,351
Heh.

270
00:19:52,399 --> 00:19:55,318
Ladies and gentlemen,
it's finally starting.

271
00:19:55,319 --> 00:19:58,154
The great race across North America.

272
00:19:58,155 --> 00:20:00,740
Steel Ball Run!

273
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:03,242
The beach is unbelievably packed

274
00:20:03,243 --> 00:20:06,663
with participants,
spectators, and horse poop.

275
00:20:07,664 --> 00:20:11,627
Now, here come the top contenders.

276
00:20:13,503 --> 00:20:17,548
The cowboy from Wyoming, Mountain Tim,

277
00:20:17,549 --> 00:20:20,802
with his beloved horse, Shadow Rider!

278
00:20:21,970 --> 00:20:26,349
The master horseman
from Mongolia, Dott Han!

279
00:20:26,350 --> 00:20:28,685
His beloved horse is Number One!

280
00:20:29,311 --> 00:20:32,772
The nomad from the Sahara, Urmd Avdul!

281
00:20:32,773 --> 00:20:35,651
Would you believe it?
He's entering on a camel!

282
00:20:36,235 --> 00:20:40,988
Now, appearing alongside
his beloved horse, Silver Bullet,

283
00:20:40,989 --> 00:20:43,699
with the saddlecloth #001,

284
00:20:43,700 --> 00:20:48,330
the nobleman of British horse racing,
Diego Brando!

285
00:20:51,375 --> 00:20:56,837
The first stage is a short ten-mile race,
with a Catholic church as the finish line.

286
00:20:56,838 --> 00:20:58,714
The winner of this stage

287
00:20:58,715 --> 00:21:02,803
will receive a one-hour time bonus
and a $10,000 prize.

288
00:21:03,303 --> 00:21:10,102
Let the Steel Ball Run begin!

289
00:21:14,398 --> 00:21:18,151
Dear distinguished guests,
after the race starts,

290
00:21:18,652 --> 00:21:23,781
you'll be able to follow it
on a specially prepared train.

291
00:21:23,782 --> 00:21:26,410
Hey, look, it's that guy.

292
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:32,708
So he really is crazy, after all.

293
00:21:39,589 --> 00:21:41,133
Damn it…

294
00:21:43,468 --> 00:21:45,137
I won't give up.

295
00:21:45,637 --> 00:21:47,346
It's the spin…

296
00:21:47,347 --> 00:21:52,143
I'm going to find out the secret
of the Steel Balls, no matter what.

297
00:21:52,144 --> 00:21:54,771
You chose the right horse.

298
00:21:55,355 --> 00:21:57,190
An old horse has experience.

299
00:21:57,691 --> 00:22:01,611
It won't rush in like a young horse
and sprain its legs.

300
00:22:02,654 --> 00:22:04,948
Since I'm intrigued, here's a hint.

301
00:22:06,074 --> 00:22:08,993
You already have the answer.

302
00:22:08,994 --> 00:22:13,623
If you have the will to ride a horse,
why don't you use it?

303
00:22:15,083 --> 00:22:16,209
He-heh!

304
00:22:18,253 --> 00:22:20,589
Two minutes until the race starts.

305
00:22:26,803 --> 00:22:28,096
One more time…

306
00:22:28,889 --> 00:22:30,640
Lick me one more time.

307
00:22:36,271 --> 00:22:37,189
One more time…

308
00:22:39,232 --> 00:22:40,108
Spin!

309
00:22:44,446 --> 00:22:47,824
It's time to start the Steel Ball Run!

310
00:23:02,589 --> 00:23:06,634
September 25, 1890, 10:00 a.m.,

311
00:23:06,635 --> 00:23:10,388
the transcontinental race
across North America, Steel Ball Run,

312
00:23:10,389 --> 00:23:12,849
has finally kicked off!

313
00:23:16,061 --> 00:23:20,732
No way! How is he controlling it
when he can't use his legs?

314
00:23:21,983 --> 00:23:24,361
I can do this if I'm with you.

315
00:23:27,406 --> 00:23:28,698
Spin…

316
00:23:29,408 --> 00:23:33,161
I want to learn more
about the Steel Balls.

317
00:23:45,799 --> 00:23:48,634
Every horse is
neck and neck from the start.

318
00:23:48,635 --> 00:23:53,097
No surprise there. The first stage may
be short, but it's still ten miles.

319
00:23:53,098 --> 00:23:57,477
A bad pace could
wear out their horses on the first day.

320
00:23:59,020 --> 00:24:01,105
Someone has jumped ahead!

321
00:24:01,106 --> 00:24:03,566
Saddlecloth #636.

322
00:24:03,567 --> 00:24:07,027
He's fast! So fast!
What unbelievable speed.

323
00:24:07,028 --> 00:24:08,112
Who's that?

324
00:24:08,113 --> 00:24:11,574
636. Gyro Zeppeli.

325
00:24:11,575 --> 00:24:15,829
Is he out of his mind?
Running at that speed on the first day…

326
00:24:16,413 --> 00:24:19,373
Is he actually planning
to cross the continent?

327
00:24:19,374 --> 00:24:24,254
No, he said he was going to win.
He came here for that reason.

328
00:24:29,718 --> 00:24:30,926
We're swerving!

329
00:24:30,927 --> 00:24:34,264
This is bad. The other horses are
starting to get riled up.

330
00:24:36,057 --> 00:24:40,020
Someone is down!
Several horses may be out already!

331
00:24:43,398 --> 00:24:46,776
However, ramming isn't against the rules.

332
00:24:47,903 --> 00:24:50,988
Another horse has
broken away from the group.

333
00:24:50,989 --> 00:24:52,990
It's Diego Brando!

334
00:24:52,991 --> 00:24:56,952
The top British racing gentleman
is making his move.

335
00:24:56,953 --> 00:25:01,458
No, wait! Someone else is also
closing in from the left rear!

336
00:25:02,751 --> 00:25:06,171
It's Urmd Avdul's camel!

337
00:25:07,422 --> 00:25:10,090
A camel weighs
1.5 times more than a horse.

338
00:25:10,091 --> 00:25:14,011
No horse can withstand this attack!

339
00:25:14,012 --> 00:25:16,264
Gyro's tripping up!

340
00:25:16,890 --> 00:25:18,975
Diego Brando seizes the opening!

341
00:25:29,110 --> 00:25:32,947
The one getting the time bonus will be

342
00:25:32,948 --> 00:25:36,033
me, Urmd Avdul!

343
00:25:36,034 --> 00:25:37,410
BOOM

344
00:25:40,288 --> 00:25:41,540
What?!

345
00:25:49,422 --> 00:25:51,507
Avdul is down!

346
00:25:51,508 --> 00:25:54,594
Didn't he notice the cactus patch?

347
00:25:55,095 --> 00:25:57,346
Avdul is unable to move!

348
00:25:57,347 --> 00:26:03,019
Urmd Avdul, a top contender,
suddenly drops out in the first stage!

349
00:26:10,402 --> 00:26:12,696
That's Gyro's Steel Ball.

350
00:26:16,533 --> 00:26:19,118
I don't get how it works,

351
00:26:19,119 --> 00:26:21,912
but he used it to locate the cactus patch

352
00:26:21,913 --> 00:26:24,457
and lure the camel rider right into it.

353
00:26:25,083 --> 00:26:29,587
I want to know
about that Steel Ball and that guy.

354
00:26:29,588 --> 00:26:33,632
I'll take whatever I can get,
except diseases.

355
00:26:33,633 --> 00:26:35,343
And especially a time bonus.

356
00:26:35,927 --> 00:26:37,429
He-heh!

357
00:26:43,852 --> 00:26:45,353
What?

358
00:26:45,937 --> 00:26:48,773
What time is it?

359
00:26:51,776 --> 00:26:55,946
What?! Dang it! I overslept!

360
00:26:55,947 --> 00:26:57,656
I can't refund your entry fee.

361
00:26:57,657 --> 00:27:01,160
No, I'm in!
I can't win the prize money otherwise!

362
00:27:01,161 --> 00:27:02,453
Say what?

363
00:27:02,454 --> 00:27:04,705
I'm gonna win, yo!

364
00:27:04,706 --> 00:27:09,793
I'm a man
at the peak of my life right now!

365
00:27:09,794 --> 00:27:14,089
Some weirdo just started.
Write it down, just in case.

366
00:27:14,090 --> 00:27:16,050
Saddlecloth #777.

367
00:27:16,051 --> 00:27:18,094
The name's Pocoloco.

368
00:27:19,763 --> 00:27:22,723
This ground is incredibly smooth!

369
00:27:22,724 --> 00:27:24,725
With horses trampling it down,

370
00:27:24,726 --> 00:27:28,312
I've never seen ground
this easy to run on!

371
00:27:28,313 --> 00:27:33,026
Pocoloco's on a roll! Yo!

372
00:27:33,777 --> 00:27:35,569
I just realized something.

373
00:27:35,570 --> 00:27:39,615
Isn't crossing the continent
with 400 yards per liter impossible?

374
00:27:39,616 --> 00:27:43,828
How unfortunate.
Let's return to our homeland, Master.

375
00:27:46,956 --> 00:27:50,084
All right,
Gyro Zeppeli still holds the lead.

376
00:27:50,085 --> 00:27:53,088
Diego Brando, known as Dio,
is holding second place.

377
00:27:54,339 --> 00:27:57,217
That guy…
He's been moving weird for a while.

378
00:27:58,009 --> 00:28:01,012
Pursuing on the right,
then closing in on the left.

379
00:28:01,513 --> 00:28:04,516
He's closing the gap with Gyro
little by little.

380
00:28:11,898 --> 00:28:15,276
Again! Did he actually find it?

381
00:28:19,030 --> 00:28:19,989
He's gone?

382
00:28:20,490 --> 00:28:23,451
What just happened? Dio has disappeared!

383
00:28:24,953 --> 00:28:27,455
He caught up to him so suddenly!

384
00:28:29,541 --> 00:28:33,877
What the hell is this?
It didn't look like he was speeding up.

385
00:28:33,878 --> 00:28:37,047
The camel thing surprised me a little,

386
00:28:37,048 --> 00:28:40,467
but now I see you as a complete amateur.

387
00:28:40,468 --> 00:28:42,429
I can read what comes next.

388
00:28:42,929 --> 00:28:46,766
So he did find it! The horse's quirk!

389
00:28:47,267 --> 00:28:52,312
Everyone and everything
has a quirk of some sort,

390
00:28:52,313 --> 00:28:54,064
horses included.

391
00:28:54,065 --> 00:28:59,153
Tail flicks before sprinting,
drifting wide when pressured,

392
00:28:59,154 --> 00:29:01,739
shaking the head, lowering the body.

393
00:29:01,740 --> 00:29:05,118
That can sometimes be
a huge weakness in a race.

394
00:29:05,618 --> 00:29:08,454
This horse's quirk is a truly fatal flaw.

395
00:29:08,455 --> 00:29:10,289
Five, six, seven…

396
00:29:10,290 --> 00:29:11,708
It shifts to the left.

397
00:29:16,129 --> 00:29:19,591
Yes, it slightly drifts
left every eighth breath.

398
00:29:20,175 --> 00:29:23,135
And naturally, this shift slows it down.

399
00:29:23,136 --> 00:29:25,846
In other words,
if I speed up at that moment,

400
00:29:25,847 --> 00:29:30,518
I can match his speed
without tiring my beloved horse!

401
00:29:32,061 --> 00:29:33,937
DASH

402
00:29:33,938 --> 00:29:36,148
Dio's in front by a head!

403
00:29:36,149 --> 00:29:38,568
What's the meaning of this?

404
00:29:39,360 --> 00:29:41,236
It's a professional technique.

405
00:29:41,237 --> 00:29:44,072
You stay back there.

406
00:29:44,073 --> 00:29:48,035
Are you saying my horse has a quirk?

407
00:29:48,036 --> 00:29:51,622
Would it matter if I told you?
You can't fix a quirk.

408
00:29:51,623 --> 00:29:53,833
Just like you can't change fate!

409
00:29:56,169 --> 00:29:58,629
Dio's advancing again!

410
00:29:58,630 --> 00:30:00,422
What is this?

411
00:30:00,423 --> 00:30:04,510
Dio takes the lead,
but it doesn't look like he's speeding up!

412
00:30:04,511 --> 00:30:08,055
Natural talent. That's what that is.

413
00:30:08,056 --> 00:30:11,517
It's no good.
He won't be able to pass him again.

414
00:30:11,518 --> 00:30:13,811
The gap will keep getting bigger.

415
00:30:13,812 --> 00:30:17,899
The sign shows we have eight miles left.
Up ahead is a dried-up river.

416
00:30:20,443 --> 00:30:25,030
Hey, so you had a quirk?
I didn't know that.

417
00:30:25,031 --> 00:30:29,327
There are some outrageously strong rivals
out there in the world.

418
00:30:29,911 --> 00:30:32,539
But you don't need to fix your quirk.

419
00:30:33,122 --> 00:30:35,542
Run and bring it out even more.

420
00:30:42,841 --> 00:30:46,802
Hey, you're wobbling. Is that your quirk?

421
00:30:46,803 --> 00:30:49,556
That's good. Do it more.

422
00:30:50,598 --> 00:30:52,976
Run and bring out your quirk even more.

423
00:30:56,604 --> 00:30:59,189
The bridge planks are
breaking and falling!

424
00:30:59,190 --> 00:31:03,027
Gyro Zeppeli charges straight through!

425
00:31:04,112 --> 00:31:05,822
Dio hesitated!

426
00:31:06,322 --> 00:31:07,240
That guy…

427
00:31:07,824 --> 00:31:10,784
The trailing riders are going
down the river.

428
00:31:10,785 --> 00:31:12,579
Dio can't cross the bridge.

429
00:31:13,079 --> 00:31:15,789
It's just like with my legs.

430
00:31:15,790 --> 00:31:21,211
The mysterious Steel Ball's spin drew out
the horse's quirk in an explosive way!

431
00:31:21,212 --> 00:31:22,630
He-heh!

432
00:31:25,884 --> 00:31:30,555
There! I see them.
I caught up to the group in the back.

433
00:31:31,806 --> 00:31:33,849
What the… It's a cliff!

434
00:31:33,850 --> 00:31:35,893
This isn't the racecourse!

435
00:31:35,894 --> 00:31:38,146
Damn it, it's that guy's fault!

436
00:31:46,279 --> 00:31:50,490
He was charging ahead so fast,
we just got drawn along!

437
00:31:50,491 --> 00:31:52,367
But look at the map!

438
00:31:52,368 --> 00:31:55,078
If we cross this cliff, it's a shortcut!

439
00:31:55,079 --> 00:31:58,040
Only if you're okay
with your horse getting hurt.

440
00:31:58,041 --> 00:32:00,501
I'm turning back. Screw this.

441
00:32:04,756 --> 00:32:06,174
I'm…

442
00:32:09,844 --> 00:32:11,888
What are you doing, Pocoloco?

443
00:32:12,847 --> 00:32:15,725
I'm counting the clouds.

444
00:32:16,309 --> 00:32:22,230
What I'm asking is
why lie around all day instead of working?

445
00:32:22,231 --> 00:32:23,815
Three days ago,

446
00:32:23,816 --> 00:32:26,443
I had an old fortune-teller lady
tell my fortune.

447
00:32:26,444 --> 00:32:27,402
So what?

448
00:32:27,403 --> 00:32:32,532
She said the worst period of one's life
is called "killed by heaven."

449
00:32:32,533 --> 00:32:33,617
Well, listen up.

450
00:32:33,618 --> 00:32:37,622
She said mine's the opposite.
The opposite of the worst.

451
00:32:38,414 --> 00:32:43,835
Your next two months will be
the most blissful period of your life.

452
00:32:43,836 --> 00:32:46,713
Moreover, you're one in five billion.

453
00:32:46,714 --> 00:32:49,174
There's nothing to hesitate about.

454
00:32:49,175 --> 00:32:52,720
No enemies to fear!

455
00:32:54,472 --> 00:32:57,182
Then here's your lucky break.

456
00:32:57,183 --> 00:33:01,061
The landlord hired us
to cultivate a new field.

457
00:33:01,062 --> 00:33:05,565
Sorry, but I decided to take it easy.

458
00:33:05,566 --> 00:33:09,278
There's no such thing
as easy for people like us.

459
00:33:09,779 --> 00:33:13,281
I lost count of the clouds.

460
00:33:13,282 --> 00:33:15,575
I negotiated with the landlord

461
00:33:15,576 --> 00:33:19,163
and got your pay bumped
from 100 to 150, you know.

462
00:33:24,168 --> 00:33:27,629
Old man, that job cultivating a new field…

463
00:33:27,630 --> 00:33:30,383
How much did you just say it pays?

464
00:33:30,883 --> 00:33:34,177
I'm a one-in-five-billion guy.

465
00:33:34,178 --> 00:33:36,847
That belief brought me here to San Diego.

466
00:33:36,848 --> 00:33:39,976
I'm going to win. I'll win, and then

467
00:33:40,560 --> 00:33:47,275
go back home
and live an even happier life!

468
00:33:55,908 --> 00:33:59,412
Use the rope you have,
if you're good with it.

469
00:34:01,122 --> 00:34:02,498
WHOOSH

470
00:34:14,218 --> 00:34:17,095
What kind of legs does that guy have?

471
00:34:17,096 --> 00:34:19,848
But I'm not thanking him.

472
00:34:19,849 --> 00:34:23,770
I made it over the cliff,
thanks to my good luck.

473
00:34:24,604 --> 00:34:26,147
Hey ya!

474
00:34:33,362 --> 00:34:36,782
Only four miles left in the first stage.

475
00:34:36,783 --> 00:34:38,950
Gyro Zeppeli is still in the lead!

476
00:34:38,951 --> 00:34:41,412
Can he hold that lead till the end?!

477
00:34:43,873 --> 00:34:49,003
Whoa, Gyro's taking a huge detour.
What on earth is he planning to do?

478
00:34:49,879 --> 00:34:51,339
It's a shortcut.

479
00:34:51,923 --> 00:34:55,884
If he charges through the woods,
he could gain about 800 yards.

480
00:34:55,885 --> 00:34:58,554
But won't those trees get in the way?

481
00:34:59,138 --> 00:35:01,891
It's a gamble. A very dangerous one.

482
00:35:02,850 --> 00:35:05,685
Now, what will the chasing pack do?

483
00:35:05,686 --> 00:35:08,564
We can't let him get any farther ahead.

484
00:35:09,148 --> 00:35:12,943
One racer followed!
Then six more. Seven racers in total!

485
00:35:12,944 --> 00:35:16,321
Yeehaw! I caught up!

486
00:35:16,322 --> 00:35:17,948
Yo!

487
00:35:17,949 --> 00:35:20,742
Do you know where the leader is right now?

488
00:35:20,743 --> 00:35:24,914
Do you even realize?
We're heading straight into the woods.

489
00:35:28,584 --> 00:35:34,215
I see. But shortcuts have
already proven to be my lucky route.

490
00:35:35,925 --> 00:35:39,387
What the… This guy's eyes are closed.

491
00:35:47,937 --> 00:35:49,396
I'm a lucky guy.

492
00:35:49,397 --> 00:35:53,650
Even if I close my eyes,
there's no way I'm hitting a tree branch.

493
00:35:53,651 --> 00:35:57,696
What's going on? It's not surprising
for a horse to keep running.

494
00:35:57,697 --> 00:36:02,243
But how can the rider stay unharmed
with his eyes closed and riding like that?

495
00:36:04,245 --> 00:36:07,915
What's up with that guy?
Why does he have his eyes closed?

496
00:36:08,416 --> 00:36:11,669
Something feels off.
With guys like that, I should just…

497
00:36:13,713 --> 00:36:14,714
Take this!

498
00:36:25,516 --> 00:36:27,435
CRUNCH

499
00:36:28,936 --> 00:36:32,315
Two minutes since they entered the woods.
Are they about to emerge?

500
00:36:33,816 --> 00:36:36,109
Here comes Gyro!

501
00:36:36,110 --> 00:36:39,738
As expected, Gyro Zeppeli
is maintaining a huge lead.

502
00:36:39,739 --> 00:36:43,492
Wait, there's another horse!
And the rider is being dragged!

503
00:36:44,160 --> 00:36:47,787
Saddlecloth #777.
Registered name is Pocoloco.

504
00:36:47,788 --> 00:36:48,788
What?

505
00:36:48,789 --> 00:36:50,123
This is unexpected.

506
00:36:50,124 --> 00:36:51,625
By being dragged along,

507
00:36:51,626 --> 00:36:54,921
he avoided the branches
and let his horse run freely!

508
00:36:56,380 --> 00:36:58,591
Was that fall actually lucky?

509
00:37:01,969 --> 00:37:05,055
I knew it! I'm truly a lucky guy!

510
00:37:05,056 --> 00:37:08,141
What the… Is that even allowed?

511
00:37:08,142 --> 00:37:10,060
Pocoloco is currently second.

512
00:37:10,061 --> 00:37:12,854
We can see the others
on the official route,

513
00:37:12,855 --> 00:37:15,065
but the gap is a few hundred yards.

514
00:37:15,066 --> 00:37:17,150
This position's not bad.

515
00:37:17,151 --> 00:37:18,903
The shortcut paid off.

516
00:37:19,528 --> 00:37:23,114
Incredible! The first stage
has been totally thrilling!

517
00:37:23,115 --> 00:37:26,368
And ahead is
the toughest part of the course,

518
00:37:26,369 --> 00:37:28,620
a 2,000-yard downhill stretch

519
00:37:28,621 --> 00:37:32,958
with a 50-yard drop
and slopes as steep as 30 degrees.

520
00:37:32,959 --> 00:37:34,084
Two thousand?

521
00:37:34,085 --> 00:37:39,048
Laying the rails was difficult,
so sadly, the train has to take a detour.

522
00:37:43,886 --> 00:37:46,972
Now, they're facing
the tricky downhill stretch.

523
00:37:46,973 --> 00:37:50,893
Needless to say, going too fast
will wreck their horses' legs.

524
00:37:51,477 --> 00:37:53,937
Every racer is holding steady.

525
00:37:53,938 --> 00:37:57,649
How they can hold steady
largely depends on a rider's skill!

526
00:37:57,650 --> 00:38:01,069
Take it slow. Careful here.

527
00:38:01,070 --> 00:38:04,657
Are you scared, Mr. One-in-Five-Billion?

528
00:38:06,784 --> 00:38:09,369
Who was that? Who said I'm scared?

529
00:38:09,370 --> 00:38:12,247
There's nothing to hesitate about.

530
00:38:12,248 --> 00:38:15,458
No enemies to fear!

531
00:38:15,459 --> 00:38:16,793
That's right.

532
00:38:16,794 --> 00:38:19,463
If there are no enemies to fear,

533
00:38:20,047 --> 00:38:22,675
then there's no road
to fear either, right?

534
00:38:25,469 --> 00:38:26,469
BAM

535
00:38:26,470 --> 00:38:28,222
Out of the way, old man!

536
00:38:28,723 --> 00:38:31,766
Pocoloco's breaking out!
He couldn't hold back!

537
00:38:31,767 --> 00:38:33,269
Go!

538
00:38:34,729 --> 00:38:37,398
Okay, he's just an idiot.

539
00:38:39,483 --> 00:38:42,068
Calm down. Don't be misled!

540
00:38:42,069 --> 00:38:47,033
They're following suit! Some of the horses
couldn't help but follow suit!

541
00:38:51,620 --> 00:38:54,372
This is terrible! It's a massive crash.

542
00:38:54,373 --> 00:38:56,583
There's a devil loose on this slope.

543
00:38:56,584 --> 00:38:58,877
It's okay! Keep going!

544
00:38:58,878 --> 00:39:00,211
We're lucky guys--

545
00:39:00,212 --> 00:39:02,256
JOLT

546
00:39:04,133 --> 00:39:05,050
WHAM

547
00:39:05,051 --> 00:39:08,053
Pocoloco's down! Gyro takes the lead!

548
00:39:08,054 --> 00:39:09,804
Nice work, pal!

549
00:39:09,805 --> 00:39:13,100
Pocoloco was foolish after all!

550
00:39:14,810 --> 00:39:16,187
What in the world?!

551
00:39:17,396 --> 00:39:18,313
What?

552
00:39:18,314 --> 00:39:21,775
Pocoloco is unharmed!
He hasn't even fallen!

553
00:39:21,776 --> 00:39:25,071
He's riding something,
and it's unbelievably fast!

554
00:39:26,614 --> 00:39:28,073
This guy…

555
00:39:28,074 --> 00:39:30,200
It's a dead body!

556
00:39:30,201 --> 00:39:32,577
He's sliding down on a cow's corpse!

557
00:39:32,578 --> 00:39:37,040
Yeehaw! Can't believe there was
a dead cow in the grass!

558
00:39:37,041 --> 00:39:38,583
I'm blown away!

559
00:39:38,584 --> 00:39:40,251
Pocoloco takes the lead!

560
00:39:40,252 --> 00:39:43,463
What is this ridiculous situation?

561
00:39:43,464 --> 00:39:46,300
Could it be some kind of ability?

562
00:39:46,926 --> 00:39:50,011
That doesn't matter right now.

563
00:39:50,012 --> 00:39:50,929
RUMBLE

564
00:39:50,930 --> 00:39:52,723
This race is meant for horses.

565
00:39:53,391 --> 00:39:56,810
You can't hop on a dead cow!

566
00:39:56,811 --> 00:39:58,104
Take this!

567
00:39:59,021 --> 00:40:00,271
CRASH

568
00:40:00,272 --> 00:40:05,152
I'll get that rock rolling
and stop the cow from sliding.

569
00:40:08,322 --> 00:40:11,075
What? Why is there a person there?

570
00:40:13,327 --> 00:40:15,161
Damn it, I missed.

571
00:40:15,162 --> 00:40:16,913
I can't believe my eyes!

572
00:40:16,914 --> 00:40:20,417
Saddlecloth #990,
Sand Man, has suddenly burst in!

573
00:40:20,418 --> 00:40:22,627
Shockingly, he's joining in on foot!

574
00:40:22,628 --> 00:40:24,672
The downhill slope is almost over.

575
00:40:26,882 --> 00:40:30,301
We're now over 17 minutes into the race!

576
00:40:30,302 --> 00:40:31,554
Damn it…

577
00:40:34,223 --> 00:40:36,683
Now, the final turn is in sight.

578
00:40:36,684 --> 00:40:39,770
After that rocky hill,
it's just a straight line!

579
00:40:40,271 --> 00:40:43,858
Wow! Sand Man is taking
a shortcut through the rocks!

580
00:40:46,444 --> 00:40:50,155
What's going on? I can't believe
things turned out like this.

581
00:40:50,156 --> 00:40:52,490
Is he even human?

582
00:40:52,491 --> 00:40:54,994
This is the natives' unknown power.

583
00:40:55,744 --> 00:40:59,664
A power perfectly suited
for a race across the continent.

584
00:40:59,665 --> 00:41:03,835
The back group finishes the descent
and heads for the final turn.

585
00:41:03,836 --> 00:41:06,964
Pocoloco is leading all 3,800 racers!

586
00:41:09,175 --> 00:41:15,889
Hey, Valkyrie, we'll never win
if we keep staring at their butts.

587
00:41:15,890 --> 00:41:17,391
Let's run.

588
00:41:20,186 --> 00:41:23,063
There he goes! Gyro's making his move!

589
00:41:24,023 --> 00:41:25,732
But isn't it too early?

590
00:41:25,733 --> 00:41:30,362
There's a 2,000-yard straightaway
after this turn!

591
00:41:42,333 --> 00:41:45,293
- Huh? So many people…
- Steel Ball Run!

592
00:41:45,294 --> 00:41:48,296
- Wow! It's a huge crowd!
- Steel Ball Run!

593
00:41:48,297 --> 00:41:50,590
The Santa Ana winds blow from Mexico

594
00:41:50,591 --> 00:41:53,718
toward the church
at the end of the desolate plains!

595
00:41:53,719 --> 00:41:58,932
Tens of thousands are flocking
to see the finish of the first stage!

596
00:41:58,933 --> 00:42:03,145
The winner of this race
will become a hero of the world.

597
00:42:06,357 --> 00:42:10,693
After running this far,
you've saved your strength well.

598
00:42:10,694 --> 00:42:13,948
We can do it. The final 2,000 yards.

599
00:42:15,533 --> 00:42:18,994
What? I can't believe it.
Who's that racer?

600
00:42:19,495 --> 00:42:20,828
It's Dio!

601
00:42:20,829 --> 00:42:25,042
Dio, who should've fallen far behind,
is now leading the chase!

602
00:42:29,838 --> 00:42:33,092
That's the wind resistance shield method!

603
00:42:33,717 --> 00:42:35,803
So he used this method to catch up.

604
00:42:36,303 --> 00:42:41,015
Winning the race or prize money
doesn't matter to me.

605
00:42:41,016 --> 00:42:46,939
But to uncover the mystery of Steel Balls,
I must make him acknowledge me.

606
00:42:47,439 --> 00:42:50,943
The one who will surpass Gyro Zeppeli…

607
00:42:52,987 --> 00:42:55,864
is me, Johnny Joestar!

608
00:42:57,908 --> 00:43:01,286
From here on out,
techniques seem to be useless.

609
00:43:01,287 --> 00:43:05,456
Only the strength left
in the legs matters for victory!

610
00:43:05,457 --> 00:43:08,167
I saved my horse's energy on the hill.

611
00:43:08,168 --> 00:43:10,044
The real race starts here.

612
00:43:10,045 --> 00:43:13,132
With less than 1,000 yards to go,
Pocoloco makes his move.

613
00:43:14,133 --> 00:43:16,884
Wow, Sand Man joins in too!

614
00:43:16,885 --> 00:43:17,802
WHOOSH

615
00:43:17,803 --> 00:43:19,262
It's that guy again.

616
00:43:19,263 --> 00:43:23,016
Five hundred yards to go.
The pursuers are charging fiercely.

617
00:43:23,017 --> 00:43:26,644
Dio and another rider,
saddlecloth #939, Johnny Joestar!

618
00:43:26,645 --> 00:43:30,315
They're seven lengths from Gyro.
Gyro is three lengths from Sand Man.

619
00:43:30,316 --> 00:43:33,151
Four racers are charging up on Sand Man!

620
00:43:33,152 --> 00:43:37,072
The pursuers are closing in on Gyro,
three lengths, two, one…

621
00:43:39,199 --> 00:43:41,743
They're neck and neck!

622
00:43:41,744 --> 00:43:44,162
Four horses are neck and neck!

623
00:43:44,163 --> 00:43:46,914
Johnny Joestar, I'm amazed.

624
00:43:46,915 --> 00:43:49,209
You've really caught up this far.

625
00:43:49,710 --> 00:43:53,379
By the way,
have you ever sailed on a ship?

626
00:43:53,380 --> 00:43:57,425
A ship goes faster
when it catches headwinds.

627
00:43:57,426 --> 00:44:02,639
The headwind from Mexico is meant
to help our horses run faster.

628
00:44:02,640 --> 00:44:04,516
From the very beginning.

629
00:44:05,601 --> 00:44:08,227
It's an intense showdown at the finish!

630
00:44:08,228 --> 00:44:11,065
Only 100 yards left!
Who will come in first?

631
00:44:14,693 --> 00:44:16,612
It's Gyro Zeppeli!

632
00:44:18,280 --> 00:44:20,698
Gyro is in the lead!

633
00:44:20,699 --> 00:44:22,575
Here he comes to take the lead!

634
00:44:22,576 --> 00:44:23,994
Those are the Steel Balls!

635
00:44:24,578 --> 00:44:30,041
He used the spin to spread his cloak
and gain lift by Bernoulli's principle.

636
00:44:30,042 --> 00:44:34,129
Just like a ship facing
the headwind from Mexico!

637
00:44:34,755 --> 00:44:37,215
Gyro is in the lead!

638
00:44:37,216 --> 00:44:39,634
Fifty yards to the goal! Thirty yards!

639
00:44:39,635 --> 00:44:43,472
No one can catch up to him!
Gyro Zeppeli is taking the lead and…

640
00:44:45,432 --> 00:44:47,267
he crossed the finish line!

641
00:44:48,936 --> 00:44:52,772
Gyro Zeppeli takes
the crown for the first stage!

642
00:44:52,773 --> 00:44:58,362
The race leader
of the Steel Ball Run is born!

643
00:44:59,655 --> 00:45:02,157
The summer of 1890.

644
00:45:02,658 --> 00:45:05,536
I was drawn here by something.

645
00:45:06,203 --> 00:45:09,957
Something beautiful
that was visible in the darkness.

646
00:45:10,457 --> 00:45:13,585
Maybe it was the light called "hope."

647
00:45:14,670 --> 00:45:18,716
This story is
about me taking my first steps.

648
00:45:19,425 --> 00:45:25,180
Not physically, but in the sense
of growing from youth into adulthood.

649
00:45:26,765 --> 00:45:33,647
It all began when I, Johnny Joestar,
met the mysterious man named Gyro Zeppeli.

650
00:47:03,570 --> 00:47:06,031
Subtitle translation by: Wataru Uno
